# An .onnx model can keep its tensor bytes out of the protobuf, in a
# neighbouring file the model names itself: each tensor's external_data
# entries carry a location, an offset and a length. onnx/src/tensor.rs's
# get_external_resources finds the location entry, takes the string form of
# its value field, joins it onto the model's directory with
# PathBuf::from(path).join(location), and hands the joined path to the data
# resolver, which opens and reads it. The model file's author therefore
# chooses the path that gets opened: an absolute location replaces the base
# outright in Path::join, and a `..` component walks the join out of the
# model directory, so a crafted model reads an arbitrary local file with
# the loader's privileges -- path traversal, CWE-22.
#
# The fixed revision walks the location's components in place and refuses anything
# that is not a Normal or CurDir component before joining.
#
# What fires without this change: nothing that discriminates. The tree
# reports two VYQL-PATH-001 rows on the File::open calls inside the data
# resolvers, but their source is a Python training script in an unrelated
# crate -- taint crossing languages through the unresolved-call bridge --
# and the same two rows survive at the fixed revision unchanged, so they carry no
# information about this defect. The honest taint chain cannot exist in
# Rust today: nothing labels the decoded protobuf as untrusted, taint dies
# in the Ok wrapper around the decode result, and the provider's
# read_bytes_from_path is a &dyn call the engine does not trace
# (callee not traced), two stops confirmed with vyql trace.
#
# Nothing is minted. The concept (code.RemoteListingDownloadPath) and the
# rule (VYQL-PATH-006) exist and cover an untrusted
# document's names becoming local path components for C, JavaScript and
# Rust's write side. The addition is the Rust binding
# vyql/bindings/rust/parsed_entry_value_path_join.vyql: a function that
# joins the string form of a parsed entry's value field onto a base path,
# with a std path materialisation in the same function and none of std's
# containment or traversal vocabulary. The consumption clause is what
# separates a path join from an iterator join taking a separator; the
# locator clause is what separates a parsed entry value from a locally
# typed name. It is the read-side complement of
# remote_uri_mirror_path_join, whose uri locator and create materialisation
# describe a mirrored write: a parsed entry value names a file being
# loaded, and the load is usually delegated to a resolver taking the path,
# so any std path consumption counts and requiring the read itself would
# miss the delegation.
#
# Measured. The vulnerable revision reports get_external_resources as
# VYQL-PATH-006 and the patched revision reports none, three --cache off
# runs each side, full tree: 4707 -> 4708 findings vulnerable, 4706 ->
# 4706 patched, the one new row at onnx/src/tensor.rs:66. The
# discrimination rides on the components() walk, std's own vocabulary, not
# on the fixed revision's names: dropping the negations makes the patched revision
# match again, and a dot-segment rejection or a strip_prefix containment
# written in place also silences it (cases c and d). Precision, enumerated
# rather than sampled: across every clone under the sibling ranks the
# value.as_str and join co-occurrence exists in exactly one file, this
# one; scanning the tough and tokio-tar trees with the binding adds no row
# (tough's single PATH-006 row predates it and is the write-side binding's
# metadata_base_url.as_str match).
#
# The offset/length half of the same fix -- the parsed offset and length
# slicing the mmap without a bounds check -- is the native-parser bounds
# family, not covered here: VYQL-MEM-005 reports the slice in both
# revisions because that rule carries no bounds-check control clause at
# all, so no fix can suppress it without a pack-level change across its
# 2642 rows on this tree alone.

test "rank1866: (a) a parsed entry's location value joined onto the model directory and delegated to a reader"
  lang rust
  file onnx/src/tensor.rs
  expect VYQL-PATH-006
  code
  ```
  use std::path::PathBuf;

  struct StringStringEntryProto {
      key: String,
      value: String,
  }

  struct TensorProto {
      external_data: Vec<StringStringEntryProto>,
  }

  fn get_external_resources(
      buf: &mut Vec<u8>,
      t: &TensorProto,
      path: &str,
  ) -> Result<(), String> {
      let location = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "location")
          .map(|it| it.value.as_str())
          .ok_or("Could not find external data location")?;

      let offset: usize = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "offset")
          .map(|it| it.value.parse())
          .transpose()
          .map_err(|_| "Error while parsing offset value")?
          .unwrap_or(0);

      let p = PathBuf::from(path).join(location);
      read_bytes_from_path(buf, &p, offset, None)?;
      Ok(())
  }
  ```

test "rank1866: (b) the patched form refuses non-normal components before joining"
  lang rust
  file onnx/src/tensor.rs
  reject VYQL-PATH-006
  code
  ```
  use std::path::PathBuf;

  struct StringStringEntryProto {
      key: String,
      value: String,
  }

  struct TensorProto {
      external_data: Vec<StringStringEntryProto>,
  }

  fn get_external_resources(
      buf: &mut Vec<u8>,
      t: &TensorProto,
      path: &str,
  ) -> Result<(), String> {
      let location = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "location")
          .map(|it| it.value.as_str())
          .ok_or("Could not find external data location")?;

      let offset: usize = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "offset")
          .map(|it| it.value.parse())
          .transpose()
          .map_err(|_| "Error while parsing offset value")?
          .unwrap_or(0);

      let location_path = std::path::Path::new(location);
      if location_path
          .components()
          .any(|c| !matches!(c, std::path::Component::Normal(_) | std::path::Component::CurDir))
      {
          return Err(format!(
              "external data location must be a relative path inside the model directory, got {location:?}"
          ));
      }

      let p = PathBuf::from(path).join(location_path);
      read_bytes_from_path(buf, &p, offset, None)?;
      Ok(())
  }
  ```

test "rank1866: (c) a dot-segment rejection written in place also silences the join"
  lang rust
  file onnx/src/tensor.rs
  reject VYQL-PATH-006
  code
  ```
  use std::path::PathBuf;

  struct StringStringEntryProto {
      key: String,
      value: String,
  }

  struct TensorProto {
      external_data: Vec<StringStringEntryProto>,
  }

  fn get_external_resources(
      buf: &mut Vec<u8>,
      t: &TensorProto,
      path: &str,
  ) -> Result<(), String> {
      let location = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "location")
          .map(|it| it.value.as_str())
          .ok_or("Could not find external data location")?;

      for segment in location.split('/') {
          if segment == "." || segment == ".." {
              return Err("external data location must stay inside the model directory".into());
          }
      }

      let p = PathBuf::from(path).join(location);
      read_bytes_from_path(buf, &p, 0, None)?;
      Ok(())
  }
  ```

test "rank1866: (d) a starts_with containment check is the same control"
  lang rust
  file onnx/src/tensor.rs
  reject VYQL-PATH-006
  code
  ```
  use std::path::PathBuf;

  struct StringStringEntryProto {
      key: String,
      value: String,
  }

  struct TensorProto {
      external_data: Vec<StringStringEntryProto>,
  }

  fn get_external_resources(
      buf: &mut Vec<u8>,
      t: &TensorProto,
      path: &str,
  ) -> Result<(), String> {
      let location = t
          .external_data
          .iter()
          .find(|it| it.key == "location")
          .map(|it| it.value.as_str())
          .ok_or("Could not find external data location")?;

      let base = PathBuf::from(path);
      let p = base.join(location);
      if !p.starts_with(&base) {
          return Err("external data location must stay inside the model directory".into());
      }
      read_bytes_from_path(buf, &p, 0, None)?;
      Ok(())
  }
  ```

